---
import LandingLayout from '@/layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import RateGrid from '@/components/site/RateGrid.astro';
import { hoursSummary } from '@/data/business';
import { rentalTerms } from '@/data/rental-terms';
import {
  assertMeta,
  assertTitle,
  carsInOrder,
  faqPage,
  fllDelivery,
  miamiDelivery,
  hubCtaSubtitle,
  itemListFor,
  publicName,
  usd,
} from '@/lib/hub';

// Every Lamborghini currently in fleet.js, STO first. A car that leaves the
// fleet drops out on the next build. The page does not state a count.
const ORDER = ['huracan-sto', 'huracan-evo', 'huracan-evo-spyder', 'lamborghini-urus'];
const lambos = carsInOrder(ORDER);
const bySlug = (slug) => lambos.find((c) => c.slug === slug);
const sto = bySlug('huracan-sto');
const evo = bySlug('huracan-evo');
const spyder = bySlug('huracan-evo-spyder');
const urus = bySlug('lamborghini-urus');
const { mileage, minimumAge, deposit } = rentalTerms;

const title = assertTitle('Lamborghini', 'Lamborghini Rental Miami | Lussaro Collection');
const description = assertMeta(
  'Lamborghini',
  `Rent a Lamborghini in Miami: Huracán STO, EVO, Spyder and Urus. Delivery is ${miamiDelivery.display} each way in Miami and ${fllDelivery.display} each way in Fort Lauderdale. 9 AM–8 PM daily.`,
);

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Which Lamborghini should I book?',
    a: [
      sto && `The Huracán STO when the drive is the point: ${sto.power} hp, rear-wheel drive, ${usd(sto.price)} a day, age ${sto.minimumAge}, and a ${sto.deposit.display} deposit. It is track-bred, street-only.`,
      evo && `The Huracán EVO at ${usd(evo.price)} a day when you want that V10 with a softer ride.`,
      spyder && `The EVO Spyder at ${usd(spyder.price)} a day when the roof has to come off.`,
      urus && `The Urus at ${usd(urus.price)} a day when people or luggage have to come too.`,
    ].filter(Boolean).join(' '),
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I put suitcases in a Huracán?',
    a: 'Barely. The STO, the EVO and the EVO Spyder have a small front compartment and no rear cargo area, so budget for a soft bag. Luggage for more than that is a job for the Urus.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is the Huracán STO for track use?',
    a: `No. The Huracán STO is track-bred, street-only. It is ${sto ? `${sto.power} hp and rear-wheel drive, ` : ''}rented for the street, with its own age and deposit.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What does delivery cost?',
    a: `A Lamborghini is ${miamiDelivery.display} each way in Miami, and ${fllDelivery.display} each way in Fort Lauderdale, and the handover point is agreed in your quote. Collection is typically the same fee as delivery.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What does a Lamborghini rental include?',
    a: `Each booking includes ${mileage.includedPerDay} miles for every day, pooled across the rental rather than capped daily. The refundable deposit is ${deposit.display}${sto?.depositDiffers ? `, except ${sto.deposit.display} on the Huracán STO` : ''}. Drivers must be ${minimumAge} or over${sto && sto.minimumAge !== minimumAge ? `, except the Huracán STO, which requires ${sto.minimumAge}` : ''}, with a valid license and insurance that covers the car. ${hoursSummary}.`,
  },
];
---
<LandingLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  h1="Lamborghini Rental in Miami"
  intro="The Lamborghini to book depends on the day. The Huracán STO is track-bred, street-only. The Huracán EVO is that V10 with a softer ride. The EVO Spyder is the open car. The Urus is the SUV."
  only={lambos.map((c) => c.slug)}
  fleetHeading="Lamborghinis in the fleet"
  fullFleetLink
  ctaTitle="Reserve your Lamborghini"
  heroImage="/cars/lamborghini-huracan-sto-rental-miami-front-quarter.jpg"
  showRating={false}
  reserveNote="Tell us the car and the dates and we'll confirm availability."
  leadNote="Prefer to talk now? Call or WhatsApp us."
  ctaSubtitle={hubCtaSubtitle}
  schema={[itemListFor(lambos), faqPage(faqs)]}
>
  <h2>Huracán STO, EVO, Spyder and Urus</h2>
  <p>Pick by the job. The figure beside each name is the 1-day price. A longer booking costs less per day, and the table under these notes is the live ladder.</p>

  {sto && (
    <>
      <h3><a href={`/cars/${sto.slug}`}>{publicName(sto)}</a> — {usd(sto.price)}/day</h3>
      <p>Track-bred, street-only: {sto.power} hp, rear-wheel drive, {sto.zeroToSixty} to 60, a fixed rear wing and a roof scoop. Two seats, a firm ride, and room for a soft bag. Minimum age {sto.minimumAge}, with a {sto.deposit.display} refundable deposit. Photos, the full rate ladder and the booking form are on the <a href={`/cars/${sto.slug}`}>Huracán STO rental in Miami</a> page.</p>
    </>
  )}

  {evo && (
    <>
      <h3><a href={`/cars/${evo.slug}`}>{publicName(evo)}</a> — {usd(evo.price)}/day</h3>
      <p>Strictly two seats, a small front trunk, and a naturally aspirated V10 with no hybrid assistance. {evo.power} hp, {evo.zeroToSixty} to 60. The front splitter sits low, so steep driveways want a slow, angled approach. It is the same engine family as the STO, with a softer ride around town.</p>
    </>
  )}

  {spyder && (
    <>
      <h3><a href={`/cars/${spyder.slug}`}>{publicName(spyder)}</a> — {usd(spyder.price)}/day</h3>
      <p>The EVO with the roof off in about seventeen seconds, at speeds up to 31 mph. {spyder.power} hp, {spyder.zeroToSixty} to 60, still two seats. Take it when the open air is the point of the booking. How that roof compares with the 911 Turbo S Cabriolet is on the <a href="/convertible-car-rental-miami">convertible car rental</a> page.</p>
    </>
  )}

  {urus && (
    <>
      <h3><a href={`/cars/${urus.slug}`}>{publicName(urus)}</a> — {usd(urus.price)}/day</h3>
      <p>Four doors, a trunk, and the ride height to clear a speed bump or a hotel ramp. A twin-turbo V8 drives all four wheels: {urus.power} hp, {urus.zeroToSixty} to 60. It is the Lamborghini that carries people and cases.</p>
    </>
  )}

  <h2>Daily rates</h2>
  <p>Each column is the per-day rate for a rental of that length. The 1-day figure is the published day rate. Longer stays read the current discount on that car, including any 3-day deal.</p>
  <RateGrid items={lambos.map((car) => ({ car, href: `/cars/${car.slug}`, name: publicName(car) }))} />

  <h2>Choosing by the day</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Luggage beyond a soft bag</strong> — Urus.</li>
    <li><strong>More than two people</strong> — Urus. A Huracán has two seats.</li>
    <li><strong>A photo or video shoot</strong> — the Huracán STO, for the wing and the shape.</li>
    <li><strong>A day where the driving is the point</strong> — Huracán STO. It is track-bred, street-only.</li>
    <li><strong>The same V10, less firm</strong> — Huracán EVO, or the EVO Spyder if the roof has to come off.</li>
    <li><strong>One car across a week of errands</strong> — Urus.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The coupes and the SF90, set beside these Huracáns, are on the <a href="/sports-car-rental-miami">sports car rental</a> page. The Urus stays on this page because it is the Lamborghini SUV, not a sports car.</p>

  <h2>Terms, briefly</h2>
  <p>Delivery is {miamiDelivery.display} each way in Miami, and {fllDelivery.display} each way in Fort Lauderdale, with the handover point agreed in your quote. {hoursSummary}. The worked figures for a Lamborghini day rate sit in the <a href="/blog/how-much-is-a-lamborghini-rental">Lamborghini rental price</a> guide, and every other number is on the <a href="/pricing">rate card</a>.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  {faqs.map((f) => (
    <>
      <h3>{f.q}</h3>
      <p>{f.a}</p>
    </>
  ))}
</LandingLayout>
